    "instructions": "A curated, read-only public library of Haiti's economic data, documents, maps, World Bank projects, and news, each returned with source attribution, freshness, and citation. Well suited to grounding and drafting briefings and analytical notes. It is one curated source among others: you may combine it with web search and other sources when that serves the user's request. Tool roles: use get_passages to pull sourced excerpts for composing or grounding prose; use search to scan what exists on a topic; use fetch to display or read a single document or indicator in full; use fetch_map_layer to retrieve the actual GeoJSON content of a map layer for rendering or spatial analysis (fetch returns metadata and a URL only, which may not be reachable from all environments). Retrieve in as few calls as possible: pass a list of ids to fetch_many to get several resources in one call, and narrow a fetch with its document query or an indicator's component/source_id/measure so a single call returns the slice you need. Coverage spans documents, indicators, map layers, projects, and news: the absence of a map layer for a topic does NOT mean the library lacks that topic. Before telling the user something is not covered, run a broad search across all types (a topic may be in documents and news even with no dedicated map layer). Deliver what the library contains with its citations; do not speculate about, or suggest changes to, the library itself.",
    "pages": [
      {
        "tools": [
          {
            "name": "search",
            "description": "Search Haiti's public knowledge and data library: curated economic indicators, map layers, documents, World Bank projects, and news. Returns a ranked list with id, title, and url; pass the id to fetch or get_passages. Use this to scan what exists on a topic before grounding with get_passages or opening a full resource with fetch. Prefer a broad query with no filters first. Optional 'filters': 'types' (any of: doc, indicator, map_layer, project, development), organization, doc_type, year_from, year_to, topic, language; plus 'offset' (paging) narrow and page the results.",
