            "name": "get_passages",
            "description": "Retrieve the document passages most relevant to a query, drawn from the full text across the public library (or within one 'doc_id'). Each passage carries its source citation and link. Use this as the primary tool to gather sourced excerpts to ground or draft a brief or note: the returned passages are cited and ready to weave into prose. CITE BY NUMBER, ONE NUMBER PER DOCUMENT: mark each claim with a bracketed number, reuse that same number for every claim drawn from the same document, and list the sources once at the end of the answer, numbered, each with its 'citation_key' and url. Do not repeat a document's full title inline.",
